  },
  {
    "text": "Burndown ChartWhat is a burndown chart and how are they used? Learn more about burndown charts and other terminology in our product management glossary.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/burndown-chart"
  },
  {
    "text": "Business AgilityBusiness agility applies the principles of agile development to the entire organization. Learn more about the benefits of business agility.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/business-agility"
  },
  {
    "text": "Business IntelligenceWhat is Business Intelligence? Business Intelligence is a method of compiling and interpreting business data to make better-informed decisions.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/business-intelligence"
  },
  {
    "text": "Business Model CanvasRead on and learn about the business canvas model. Also, use our resource library to learn more product management terminology.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/business-model-canvas"
  },
  {
    "text": "Business TransformationBusiness transformation is an umbrella term for making fundamental changes in how a business or organization runs.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/business-transformation"
  },
  {
    "text": "Buy-a-FeatureHow can you prioritize product initiatives with buy-a-feature activities? Find out in our step-by-step guide to buy-a-feature prioritization.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/buy-a-feature"
  },
  {
    "text": "Buyer PersonaA buyer persona represents the combined attributes of a broad cohort of individuals who have a say in the purchasing process.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/buyer-persona"
  },
  {
    "text": "CannibalizationWhat is product Cannibalization? Learn more about Cannibalization and other product management terminology in our resources library.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/cannibalization"
  },
  {
    "text": "Captive Product PricingCaptive product pricing is a pricing strategy to attract a large volume of customers to purchase a core product once that has accessories.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/what-is-captive-product-pricing"
  },
  {
    "text": "Certified Product ManagerA certified product manager is a PM who has completed an education program from a product industry organization.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/certified-product-manager"
  },
  {
    "text": "Change EnablementChange enablement, called change management, refers to providing people with the necessary information and support\u2013alongside tools, processes, and strategies\u2013 to help them adapt and transition to change within an organization.Whether it be crisis-driven change to avert disaster, transformation change, or organization-wide change to enable growth, the need for transition will impact every organization at some point. Change enablement helps organizations and teams successfully manage these changes.But how do change enablement and change management differ?",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/change-enablement"
  },
  {
    "text": "Change ManagementLearn how change management refers to a systematic approach to supporting employees and teams through transitions to new processes or tools.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/change-management"
  },
  {
    "text": "Change Management PrinciplesWhat are the 7 change management principles that help create change and manage disruptions within an organization?",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/change-management-principles"
  },
  {
    "text": "Channels of DistributionA channel of distribution is the method a company uses to get a product or service into the hands of a consumer as efficiently as possible.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/channels-of-distribution"
  },
  {
    "text": "Chief Product OfficerA chief product officer (CPO) is an executive who leads the entire product organization. Read to find the key objectives of a CPO and how to become one.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/chief-product-officer"
  },
  {
    "text": "ChurnChurn measures the percentage of accounts that cancel or do not renew their subscription, often indicating a level of product dissatisfaction.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/churn"
  },
  {
    "text": "CIRCLES MethodThe CIRCLES method is a problem-solving framework that helps product managers (PMs) make an informed response to any design question.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/circles-method"
  },
  {
    "text": "Competitive Intelligence",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/competitive-intelligence"
  },
  {
    "text": "Competitive LandscapeThe competitive landscape refers to the list of options a customer could choose rather than your product. The list includes your competitors\u2019 products and other types of customer solutions. A customer might also choose to purchase a product.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/competitive-landscape"
  },
  {
    "text": "Concept ReviewWhat is a concept review? Learn more about this term in our product management glossary and how it's important to product teams.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/concept-review"
  },
  {
    "text": "Continuous DeliveryContinuous delivery is the ability to deploy changes to software frequently and is a prerequisite for continuous deployment.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/continuous-delivery"
  },
  {
    "text": "Continuous DeploymentWhat is Continuous Deployment? Define this software product development strategy and learn the common practices associated with it.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/continuous-deployment"
  },
  {
    "text": "Continuous ImprovementContinuous improvement is a company culture that encourages all employees to look for ways to enhance the business\u2019s operations. This includes suggesting ideas to improve efficiencies, evaluating current processes, and finding opportunities to cut unproductive work.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/continuous-improvement"
  },
  {
    "text": "Continuous IntegrationContinuous integration or CI, refers to an engineering practice that is said to help automate certain pieces of work and identify bugs early in the process. Engineers practicing continuous integration merge their code to a shared repository several times each day. That code is then passed through several automated tests to help identify any errors.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/continuous-integration"
  },
  {
    "text": "Cost of DelayWhat is Cost of Delay? Learn how you can use cost of delay to efficiently prioritize your team's work and estimate value in your initiatives.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/cost-of-delay"
  },
  {
    "text": "Cross-Functional TeamWhat does a cross-functional team mean? Learn what it is and who might be in an example cross-functional agile product management team.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/cross-functional-team"
  },
  {
    "text": "Crystal Agile FrameworkWhat is the crystal framework for agile product development? Here is a broad overview of this agile framework and its strengths and weaknesses.",
    "url": "https://www.productplan.com/glossary/crystal-agile-framework"
  },
